---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const path = '/terms/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use for DocuForge Tools Generators"
  description="Terms of use for DocuForge Tools free document generators: no warranty, not legal advice, acceptable use, and limits of liability for editable templates."
  path={path}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Terms', path }]} />
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="content-meta">Last updated: 2026-10-24</p>
  <p class="lead">
    By using {siteConfig.siteName}, you agree to these terms. The site provides free browser-based
    document generators and educational articles only.
  </p>

  <h2>Service description</h2>
  <p>
    We provide free, client-side document generators (estimates, invoices, contracts, forms, and
    creative templates) plus supporting guides. Tools run in your browser; optional drafts may be
    stored in localStorage on your device. We may change, add, or remove tools and content at any
    time without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>No legal, tax, or professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Contract, NDA, vendor, consent, rental, and similar content is general information and editable
    sample language only. It is not legal, tax, medical, accounting, or other professional advice,
    and it is not a substitute for advice from a licensed professional in your jurisdiction. Do not
    treat any generated document as attorney-reviewed or guaranteed to be enforceable.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    You are solely responsible for reviewing, editing, and validating every exported document before
    you use it; complying with applicable laws, licenses, and industry rules; obtaining required
    signatures, disclosures, and insurance; and deciding whether counsel should review a draft.
    Examples and defaults on this site are illustrative only.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    You may use the site for lawful personal or business document drafting. You must not abuse the
    service, attempt unauthorized access, interfere with other users, scrape in a way that degrades
    availability, upload malware, or use the tools to create fraudulent, deceptive, or illegal
    documents. We may block access that threatens site stability or other users.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Site branding, original guides, and software are owned by {siteConfig.siteName} or its licensors.
    You retain rights in the content you enter into generators. You may export and use documents you
    create for your own business, subject to these terms and any third-party rights in your inputs.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The site and all generators are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any
    kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and
    non-infringement. We do not warrant that exports are error-free, complete, or suitable for any
    specific transaction.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {siteConfig.siteName} and its maintainer are not liable
    for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost
    profits, data, goodwill, or business opportunity, arising from your use of the site or exported
    files—even if advised of the possibility. Our total liability for any claim relating to the site
    is limited to the greater of (a) amounts you paid us for the service in the twelve months before
    the claim (currently $0 for the free tools) or (b) fifty U.S. dollars ($50).
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> page describe
    analytics cookies and how form data is handled (client-side processing; no server-side storage of
    your document text). Review those pages for consent and retention details.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms by posting a revised version with a new “Last updated” date. Continued
    use after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms:
    <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
    or use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
